.SH HISTORY
.B leafdump
is a direct descendant of
.BR json_dump.pl ,
a Perl script its author wrote and used daily for several years \(em and would
probably still be using, had Perl stayed as ubiquitous on a fresh machine as it
once was.  The rewrite exists because that assumption stopped holding, not
because the notation needed fixing: the default output is the same notation for
the same reason, and
.B \-\-perl\-compat
reproduces the original byte for byte, quirks included.  The Perl script is
kept in the source tree, where the test suite runs it alongside the rewrite and
compares the two line for line.
